# The people who may log in. scripts/make_users.py packs this into the
# binary table auth serves from (specs/auth.md); the initrd carries the
# table as users.db.
#
# One row per user: name, secret, account (defaults to the name), home
# (defaults to Sys:Homes/<name>; a name that is not a clean FAT 8.3 needs
# an explicit one). The
# secret is the plain word, honestly interim until login becomes a
# challenge -- this one is the development credential, not a real one.
# One row per user: name, secret, account (defaults to the name), home.
# The home is the row's own statement -- the convention Sys:Homes/<name> is
# only the packer's default; auth reads whatever the row says (specs/auth.md).
name=rroland secret=aegir account=rroland home=Sys:Homes/rroland
# A second user, for the ownership arc's denial: bar's home is bar's, and
# rroland's session must not reach it through the public Sys: (specs/ownership.md).
name=bar secret=bar account=bar home=Sys:Homes/bar
